0,Khoe–Kwadi languages - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khoe–Kwadi_languages,"The Khoe–Kwadi languages are a family consisting of the Khoe languages of southern Africa and the poorly attested extinct Kwadi language of Angola. The relationship has been worked out by Tom Güldemann, Edward Elderkin, and Anne-Maria Fehn.",ǁGana,Khoe-Kwadi
1,Khoe languages - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khoe_languages,"The Khoe languages were once considered to be a branch of a Khoisan language family, and were known as Central Khoisan in that scenario. Though Khoisan is now rejected as a family, the name is retained as a term of convenience. The nearest relative of the Khoe family may be the extinct Kwadi language of Angola. This larger group, for which pronouns and some basic vocabulary have been ...",ǁGana,Khoe-Kwadi
